The base class members Logger, LibraryManager, and FileSystem are not virtual, so I cannot override them in a test subclass to inject mocks. Also, the refactor tool is not available to add virtual or interface seams.

I will write a test that uses Moq to create a mock ILogger and then use reflection or other means to invoke the private RefreshMetadataForOwnedVideo method to trigger the log call. I will also mock the LibraryManager and FileSystem dependencies by setting them via reflection or other means if possible.

I will submit a test that covers the Logger.LogInformation call on line 532 by invoking the private method indirectly through the public method RefreshMetadataForOwnedVideo with the right parameters and mocks.

